<title>USA: Fay's antitrust waiting period expires.</title>
<headline>Fay's antitrust waiting period expires.</headline>
<dateline>LIVERPOOL, N.Y. 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fay's Inc said on Monday that the waiting period under the Hart-Scott-Rodino Antitrust Improvements Act of 1976 has expired for J.C. Penney Co Inc's Inc's pending $285 million acquisition Fay's.</p>
<p>Fay's also said that proxy materials have been mailed to its shareholders of record as of August 30, 1996 for an October 11, 1996 special meeting of shareholders at which the J.C. Penney transaction will be considered.</p>
<p>If the shareholders approve the deal, Fay's said it presently anticipates that the transaction will be consummated about October 11, 1996.</p>
</text>
